Name the i386 jmp_buf struct so C++ modules can export it.

GCC 16 compiles libstdc++'s C++23 std module with -fmodules. On i386,
newlib declares jmp_buf as a typedef of an unnamed struct. An unnamed
struct has no linkage, so C++ modules treat it as local to one
translation unit and refuse to export it:

  setjmp-dj.h:34:3: error: 'jmp_buf' exposes TU-local entity 'struct<unnamed>'

libstdc++'s makefile does not stop there. It prints "Cannot compile std
module", replaces std.cc with an empty file and keeps going, so
gcm.cache/std.gcm is never written and std.compat cannot import it.
Nothing later reports a problem, so the toolchain can finish building
with no working std module.

Naming the struct gives it linkage. The layout and the ABI do not change.

Only i386 is affected. On x86_64 newlib defines jmp_buf as an array of
long long, which already has linkage.

--- a/newlib/libc/include/machine/setjmp-dj.h
+++ b/newlib/libc/include/machine/setjmp-dj.h
@@ -21,7 +21,7 @@
 extern "C" {
 #endif
 
-typedef struct {
+typedef struct __jmp_buf_i386 {
   unsigned long eax;
   unsigned long ebx;
   unsigned long ecx;
